  <title>Statements</title>

  <p>A statement shows a customer what they owed at the end of the last
  statement, and every invoice, credit memo and payment since. Open
  <guiseq><gui>Customer</gui><gui>Statements</gui></guiseq>, the
  <gui>Customer Statement</gui> button of the main window, or double click
  <gui>Print statements</gui> in the main window's to-do list.</p>

  <steps>
    <item><p>In the calendar beside <gui>Statement to Date</gui>, double click
    the last day the statements cover, usually the last day of the
    month.</p></item>
    <item><p>Choose a customer. Only customers whose account is not at zero
    are listed. The window shows their balance on the statement date and
    their whole account balance today.</p></item>
    <item><p>Check the lines, and click <gui>View statement</gui> to see it
    before printing.</p></item>
    <item><p>Click <gui>Print statement</gui>. The customer is taken off the
    list, and the next customer can be chosen.</p></item>
    <item><p>When every statement is printed, click <gui>Finish
    statements</gui>. <gui>Print statements</gui> leaves the main window's
    to-do list until next month.</p></item>
  </steps>

  <note><p><gui>Print statement</gui> closes the statement even if the print
  dialog is cancelled: its lines will not appear on the next statement,
  which starts from this one's balance. Use <gui>View statement</gui> to
  check it first.</p></note>

  <p><gui>Add payment</gui> opens <link xref="customer_payment"/> for the
  chosen customer, to record a payment before printing. Statements already
  printed can be found again in <link xref="customer_statements"/>.</p>

</page>
